      "body": "### Go version\n\ngo version go1.28-devel_1e963f8291 Tue Sep 29 19:55:20 2026 -0700 linux/amd64\n\n### Output of `go env` in your module/workspace:\n\n```shell\nAR='ar'\nCC='gcc'\nCGO_CFLAGS='-O2 -g'\nCGO_CPPFLAGS=''\nCGO_CXXFLAGS='-O2 -g'\nCGO_ENABLED='1'\nCGO_FFLAGS='-O2 -g'\nCGO_LDFLAGS='-O2 -g'\nCXX='g++'\nGCCGO='gccgo'\nGO111MODULE=''\nGOAMD64='v1'\nGOARCH='amd64'\nGOAUTH='netrc'\nGOBIN='/home/cuonglm/go/bin'\nGOCACHE='/home/cuonglm/.cache/go-build'\nGOCACHEPROG=''\nGODEBUG=''\nGOENV='/home/cuonglm/.config/go/env'\nGOEXE=''\nGOEXPERIMENT=''\nGOFIPS140='off'\nGOFLAGS=''\nGOGCCFLAGS='-fPIC -m64 -pthread -Wl,--no-gc-sections -fmessage-length=0 -ffile-prefix-map=/tmp/go-build2435270519=/tmp/go-build -gno-record-gcc-switches'\nGOHOSTARCH='amd64'\nGOHOSTOS='linux'\nGOINSECURE=''\nGOMOD='/dev/null'\nGOMODCACHE='/home/cuonglm/go/pkg/mod'\nGONOPROXY=''\nGONOSUMDB=''\nGOOS='linux'\nGOPACKAGESDRIVER=''\nGOPATH='/home/cuonglm/go'\nGOPRIVATE=''\nGOPROXY='https://proxy.golang.org,direct'\nGOROOT='/home/cuonglm/sources/go'\nGOSUMDB='sum.golang.org'\nGOTELEMETRY='local'\nGOTELEMETRYDIR='/home/cuonglm/.config/go/telemetry'\nGOTMPDIR=''\nGOTOOLCHAIN='auto'\nGOTOOLDIR='/home/cuonglm/sources/go/pkg/tool/linux_amd64'\nGOVCS=''\nGOVERSION='go1.28-devel_1e963f8291 Tue Sep 29 19:55:20 2026 -0700'\nGOWORK=''\nPKG_CONFIG='pkg-config'\n```\n\n### What did you do?\n\nCompile a variadic function whose body depends on SIMD, with `GOEXPERIMENT=simd`.\n\nThere are two symptoms depending on the element type of the variadic parameter.\n\n```go\n//go:build goexperiment.simd\n\npackage main\n\nimport (\n\t\"fmt\"\n\t\"simd\"\n)\n\nfunc f(xs ...any) int {\n\tv := simd.BroadcastUint8s(' ')\n\tp := make([]byte, 4)\n\tv.StorePart(p)\n\treturn len(xs)\n}\n\nfunc main() {\n\tfmt.Println(\"len(xs) =\", f(1, 2, 3), \"want 3\")\n}\n```\n```go\n//go:build goexperiment.simd\n\npackage main\n\nimport \"simd\"\n\nfunc f(xs ...int) int {\n\tv := simd.BroadcastUint8s(' ')\n\tp := make([]byte, 4)\n\tv.StorePart(p)\n\treturn len(xs)\n}\n\nfunc main() {\n\tprintln(f(1, 2, 3))\n}\n```\n\n\n\n### What did you see happen?\n\nCase 1 compiles and prints the wrong answer:\n\n```\nlen(xs) = 1 want 3\n```\n\nCase 2 fails to compile, once per size variant:\n\n```\n./main.go:7:8: cannot use xs (variable of type []int) as int value in argument to f@simd0\n./main.go:7:8: cannot use xs (variable of type []int) as int value in argument to f@simd128\n./main.go:7:8: cannot use xs (variable of type []int) as int value in argument to f@simd256\n./main.go:7:8: cannot use xs (variable of type []int) as int value in argument to f@simd512\n```\n\n### What did you expect to see?\n\nBoth programs behave as they do without the simd experiment.",
